WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.073
Meet CrossExam.

2
00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:07.044
It finds broken software that your tests accept, then proves whether stronger evaluations actually help.

3
00:00:07.295 --> 00:00:09.154
Here, all four tests pass.

4
00:00:09.369 --> 00:00:12.122
But an optimization drops the tenant from the cache key.

5
00:00:12.373 --> 00:00:17.164
Two customers reuse the same request ID, and the second gets the first customer's reservation.

6
00:00:17.593 --> 00:00:20.239
CrossExam reduces the failure to two requests.

7
00:00:20.454 --> 00:00:22.814
The eval improves through versioned proposals.

8
00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:28.106
Each suite is frozen, then challenged on separate validation defects and correct implementations.

9
00:00:28.321 --> 00:00:30.109
Only measured gains earn promotion.

10
00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:32.540
A deliberately weakened suite is rejected.

11
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.579
Now the final audit opens.

12
00:00:34.757 --> 00:00:39.835
Detection rises from 1 of 8 defects to 7 of 8, with 0 correct controls rejected.

13
00:00:40.264 --> 00:00:43.053
Every result, including remaining misses, is published.

14
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:46.772
Subquadratic prioritizes risks from repository context.

15
00:00:47.201 --> 00:00:49.562
This run uses local attack and test fixtures.

16
00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:52.387
OpenUI makes every result inspectable.

17
00:00:52.637 --> 00:00:53.352
CrossExam.

18
00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:54.818
Your tests passed.

19
00:00:54.997 --> 00:00:56.070
Your software failed.

20
00:00:56.499 --> 00:00:57.572
Here is the evidence.
